@startuml deployment
!include _style.puml
title PandaStore - Configuration-Supported Deployment Topology
left to right direction

node "Client device" as Client {
  artifact "Web browser\nReact application" as Browser
}
node "Frontend runtime\nNode.js / Next.js\nDevelopment :3000" as Frontend {
  artifact "frontend/\nPages, API route handlers,\nServer Actions, middleware" as FrontendApp
}
node "Backend runtime\nJava 21 / Spring Boot\nPORT default :8080" as Backend {
  artifact "backend JAR\nEmbedded Tomcat / REST API\nSpring Security / JPA" as BackendApp
}
node "Configured PostgreSQL endpoint\nSelf-hosted or Supabase database" as DBHost {
  database "DB_URL-selected database\npublic schema / 21 tables" as DB
}
cloud "UploadThing service\nExternal HTTPS endpoints" as Upload {
  artifact "Upload API / callbacks\nStored product images\nSeller document images" as Files
}
node "Optional local template service\njson-server :5000" as Template {
  artifact "frontend/db.json" as TemplateData
}

Browser --> FrontendApp : HTTP :3000 in development\nHTTPS at configured public origin in production
FrontendApp --> BackendApp : HTTP :8080 by default\nBACKEND_API_URL selects HTTP(S) endpoint\nJSON / Bearer JWT
BackendApp --> DB : JDBC PostgreSQL over TCP\nHost, port and TLS from DB_URL
FrontendApp --> Files : HTTPS :443\nUploadThing SDK control / deletion
Browser --> Files : HTTPS :443\nUpload / image delivery
Files --> FrontendApp : HTTPS callback to configured app URL
FrontendApp ..> TemplateData : HTTP :5000\ngetProducts() fallback

note bottom of Frontend
  BACKEND_API_URL defaults to http://localhost:8080.
  ALLOWED_REQUEST_ORIGINS governs mutation origins.
  Browser session is an auth_token HttpOnly cookie;
  Secure flag is enabled when NODE_ENV=production.
  UploadThing credentials remain server-side.
end note
note bottom of Backend
  server.port=${PORT:8080}; database credentials
  use DB_URL, DB_USERNAME and DB_PASSWORD.
  JWT signing secret uses JWT_SECRET.
  CORS uses exact ALLOWED_REQUEST_ORIGINS
  (default http://localhost:3000).
end note
note bottom of DBHost
  A Supabase-hosted PostgreSQL database is compatible
  with backend/db/supabase-schema.sql.
  Database port/TLS are not hard-coded in the repository.
  The configured login role is not verified by this diagram.
end note
legend bottom
  Supported topology inferred from code/configuration, not a verified production deployment.
  Nodes may share one development machine; no actual hostnames, replicas,
  reverse proxy, container platform, payment gateway or courier integration are asserted.
  Sources: backend/src/main/resources/application.properties, backend/pom.xml,
  frontend/package.json, frontend route handlers and UploadThing configuration.
endlegend
@enduml
